    "scholarships": "• Steghub 100% Free DevOps/Cloud Engineering Scholarship: Provides full training, mentorship, and a free AWS certification.n  • Linux Foundation Training (LiFT) Scholarships: Covers the cost of training and certification exams for Kubernetes and Linux.n  • Amazon Future Engineer Scholarship: Offers up to $40,000 for computer science and engineering degrees, including software and computer engineering tracks.n  • AWS AI and ML Scholarship: A fully funded Udacity Nanodegree program focused on AI and machine learning for career switchers and students.n  • Generation Google Scholarship: A $10,000 award for computer science and software engineering students, aligning with SRE and infrastructure paths.n  • ISACA Foundation Academic Scholarships: Financial aid for students in IT audit and cybersecurity, relevant for cloud governance and GRC roles.n  • DoD SMART Scholarship: Full tuition and a stipend for students in systems and cloud security in exchange for guaranteed job placement.n  • (ISC)2 Undergraduate and Graduate Scholarships: Funding between $1,000 and $5,000 for cybersecurity and DevSecOps tracks.n  • Knixat Scholarship: Focused on training aspiring DevOps enthusiasts to become proficient engineers.n  • Merit• cum• Means Based Scholarship: Awarded by the Ministry of Minority Affairs, covering full course fees for eligible engineering students.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Earn a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Technology, or a related field to learn programming, operating systems, and software development.n2.  Gain experience in a developer or operations role, such as a System Administrator, to understand the software development life cycle and infrastructure.n3.  Master technical skills including Linux fundamentals, shell scripting, and version control using Git.n4.  Learn automation and configuration management tools like Ansible, Terraform, Puppet, or Chef.n5.  Understand containerization and orchestration using Docker and Kubernetes.n6.  Build proficiency in CI/CD pipelines using tools like Jenkins, GitHub Actions, or Azure Pipelines.n7.  Pursue industry certifications such as AWS Certified DevOps Engineer, Google Professional Cloud DevOps Engineer, or Microsoft Certified: DevOps Engineer Expert to validate your expertise.",
