    "scholarships": "• True North Scholarship India: A scholarship provided by Bain & Company for women in their penultimate year of undergraduate university. Winners receive INR 75,000 and an interview for an associate consultant position.n  • S3G Advisors NextGen Scholarship: A $500 scholarship for students planning to forge their own paths through leadership, community service, or volunteer work.n  • Prosci JJ Johnson Scholarship: A scholarship for United States residents covering a three• day Change Management Certification Program, awarded based on financial need.n  • AACE International Scholarship: Awards up to $2,500 for business majors dedicated to pursuing careers in cost management or cost engineering.n  • Investments & Wealth Foundation Scholarships: Covers certification programs like CIMA® for underrepresented groups, with awards at institutions like Yale School of Management ranging from $2,000 to $2,250.n  • IMA Memorial Education Fund (MEF) Scholarship: Awards ranging from $1,000 to $2,500 for students pursuing careers in management accounting or financial management.n  • Stuart Cameron & Margaret McLeod Memorial Scholarship (SCMS): A $5,000 scholarship for IMA student members pursuing management accounting.n  • CIAM Merit and Achievement Scholarships: Tuition• only scholarships for students at the California Institute of Advanced Management who demonstrate academic or professional excellence.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in any stream, though Science or Commerce is often preferred for analytical roles.n2.  Complete a Bachelor's degree. While a degree in any subject is often acceptable, fields such as Business, Economics, Finance, Accounting, Management, Engineering, or Mathematics are highly recommended.n3.  Gain professional experience through internships, fellowships, or entry• level positions in corporate departments or consulting firms to build commercial awareness and leadership skills.n4.  Optional: Pursue a Master's degree, such as an MBA or a specialized Master's in Management, Consulting, or Project Management, to gain a competitive edge for senior roles.n5.  Optional: Obtain professional certifications like Certified Management Consultant (CMC), Project Management Professional (PMP), or Certified Manager (CM) to verify credentials and upgrade skills.n6.  Alternative Route: Apply for a Higher Apprenticeship (Level 4) or a Degree Apprenticeship (Level 6) in Junior Management Consulting or Chartered Management to work while studying.",
