    "scholarships": "• Behavioral Health Scholarship Program: Provides up to $35,000 for students becoming licensed behavioral health professionals who commit to a 12• month service obligation in California's underserved areas.n  • NBCC Minority Fellowship Program: Offers up to $20,000 to master's• level minority fellows committed to serving underserved populations.n  • Chandler Wall Memorial Scholarship: A $15,000 award for undergraduate students in Arkansas pursuing social work or mental health.n  • Sharon Stephens Brehm Undergraduate Psychology Scholarship: Provides $5,000 to undergraduate psychology students with a minimum 3.5 GPA and financial need.n  • The Melanie Foundation Scholarship: Awards $2,500 to graduate students in a mental health field who demonstrate compassion and leadership.n  • NBCC Foundation Rural Scholarship: An $8,000 scholarship for students in CACREP• accredited programs who commit to serving rural populations for at least two years.n  • \"Hope for Healing\" Scholarship: A $5,000 award for undergraduate students studying mental or behavioral health with a minimum 3.0 GPA.n  • Behavioral Health Academic Scholarship: A $5,000 scholarship from American Addiction Centers for students in social work, psychology, or counseling.n  • Future Mental Health Professional Scholarship Program: Provides $2,000 to students pursuing a career in the mental health field.n  • NBCC Foundation Military Scholarship: Available to master's• level counseling students committed to serving military• connected communities.",
    "educationPath": "To become a Licensed Mental Health Counselor, you typically follow these steps:  • Complete a bachelor's degree in a behavioral, social science, or psychology field (approx. 4 years).n  • Earn a master's degree in mental health counseling or a related field, such as Clinical Mental Health Counseling, Marriage and Family Therapy, or Social Work (approx. 2• 3 years). Ensure the program is accredited, such as by CACREP.n  • Complete graduate supervised counseling experience, including a practicum (approx. 100 hours) and an internship (approx. 600 hours).n  • Complete post• graduate supervised clinical experience, which typically requires 2,000 to 4,000 hours depending on state requirements.n  • Pass required national or state licensing examinations, such as the National Counselor Examination (NCE) or the National Clinical Mental Health Counseling Examination (NCMHCE).n  • Apply for and maintain state licensure through ongoing continuing education.",
