    "scholarships": "• Digiteum Internet of Things (IoT) Scholarship: Provides $2,000 or £1,600 to undergraduate and graduate students in the U.S. and U.K. studying engineering or computer science.n  • Wisconsin IoT Council Scholarships: Offers tuition awards up to $2,000 for students at member institutions in Wisconsin pursuing degrees or certifications in the IoT and manufacturing space.n  • Zipit Wireless Future of Connectivity Scholarship: A $2,500 essay• based scholarship for undergraduate or graduate students interested in the future of connectivity and IoT.n  • SMART Scholarship• for• Service: A Department of Defense program providing full tuition, stipends, and employment for STEM students in fields like electrical engineering and computer science that overlap with IoT.n  • ISA Smart Manufacturing and IIoT Division Scholarship: Specifically targets students interested in industrial IoT and smart manufacturing.n  • AFCEA STEM Majors Scholarship: Provides $2,500 to undergraduates in fields including electronics and telecommunications engineering, which are foundational to IoT.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 with a focus on Science, Mathematics, and Computer Science.n2.  Earn a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, or Information Technology. Specialized B.Tech or BS programs in Internet of Things (IoT) are also available.n3.  Pursue a Master's degree or Ph.D. in Computer Science or a related field to specialize in senior roles such as IoT Solutions Architect.n4.  Obtain professional certifications to enhance credibility, such as Certified Internet of Things Practitioner (CIoTP), Microsoft Certified: Azure IoT Developer Specialty, AWS Certified Solutions Architect, or Google Cloud Professional IoT Engineer.n5.  Gain practical experience through internships, personal projects (e.g., building prototypes with Arduino or Raspberry Pi), and contributing to open• source IoT platforms.n6.  Develop core technical skills in programming (C, C++, Python, Java, JavaScript), embedded systems, networking protocols (MQTT, HTTP, TCP/IP), cloud computing, and data analytics.n7.  Stay updated with industry trends by attending workshops, conferences, and reading specialized IoT publications.",
