    "traits": "• Curiosity and creativityn  • Openness to being wrong and patiencen  • Perseverance after failuren  • Critical thinking and skepticismn  • Persistencen  • Honesty and ethicsn  • Openness to feedbackn  • Collaboration and leadershipn  • Willingness to learnn  • Research tasten  • Systematic writing habits",
    "courseFees": "AI safety researcher course fees vary widely by program type:  • Many foundational courses are free or \"pay• what• you• want\"n  • Professional certifications typically range from USD 1,899 to USD 2,799n  • Advanced technical certifications can cost between USD 2,000 and USD 8,000n  • Comprehensive bootcamps and specialized university• level programs range from USD 2,400 to over USD 20,000 per year",
    "scholarships": "• Anthropic Fellows Program: Funding and mentorship for engineers and researchers to investigate high• priority AI safety research questions.n  • Singapore AI Safety Fellowship (SASH): Fully funded 3• month in• person program in Singapore for emerging researchers, including a stipend and up to $30,000 research compute.n  • Global AI Safety Fellowship: Fully funded research program for up to 6 months for STEM talent, providing up to $30,000 to cover salary and living expenses.n  • Cambridge Boston Alignment Initiative (CBAI) Summer Research Fellowship: Fully funded nine• week intensive program in Cambridge, Massachusetts, for aspiring AI safety researchers.n  • Schmidt Sciences AI2050 Fellowships: Multi• year fellowships for early• career researchers working on transformative AI safety and beneficial AI challenges.n  • BASE Fellows: 13• week remote program for Black researchers and students focusing on AI safety, security, and governance.n  • AISAR Program: Six• month fellowship for Argentine researchers and students with a monthly stipend and compute budget.n  • ML Safety Research Scholarship: $2,000 for undergraduates and masters students who secure ML safety research mentorship.n  • OpenAI Safety Fellowship: Opportunity for AI researchers to work on safe and ethical AI alignment.n  • International Programme on AI Evaluation: Fully funded hybrid programme focused on AI capabilities and safety evaluation.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in the Science stream with a strong focus on Mathematics.n2.  Complete a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Mathematics, Statistics, Physics, or Engineering. Ensure high proficiency in Python programming, calculus, linear algebra, and probability.n3.  (Optional but recommended) Gain early research experience through internships, summer programs (like AI Safety Camp or MATS), or by contributing to open• source safety projects.n4.  Pursue a Master's degree or PhD in Machine Learning, Computer Science, or a related quantitative field like Cognitive Science. A PhD is generally the best path for becoming a research lead.n5.  Supplement technical studies with coursework in Philosophy (ethics), Economics, and AI Governance to understand the societal and moral implications of AI.n6.  Build a portfolio by replicating papers, developing evaluation tools, or publishing independent research on platforms like the Alignment Forum or LessWrong.n7.  Network and stay updated by attending major conferences such as NeurIPS or ICML and participating in specialized AI safety workshops.",
