    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in any stream, though a background in psychology, communications, or computer science is helpful.n2.  Pursue a Bachelor's degree in fields such as Linguistics, Psychology, UX Design, Communications, Creative Writing, or Computer Science.n3.  Gain specialized skills through online courses or bootcamps focused on Conversation Design, Natural Language Processing (NLP), and AI frameworks.n4.  Obtain industry• recognized certifications, such as the CDI Method Foundation, Conversation Designer (CXD1), or AI Trainer (AIT1) from the Conversation Design Institute.n5.  Master conversation design tools like Voiceflow, Dialogflow, Rasa, or GPT• based platforms to create interactive prototypes.n6.  Build a portfolio by designing sample chatbot scripts, mapping user flows, and creating prototypes to demonstrate practical expertise.n7.  Seek practical experience through internships, freelance projects, or entry• level roles in tech firms or agencies.",
