    "traits": "• You are curious and have a natural drive to understand the \"why\" behind anomaliesn  • You are resilient and persistent when handling high• stakes incidents and constant pressuren  • You have a hacker mindset and like to think outside the box to anticipate problemsn  • You are adaptable and willing to learn as systems and threats changen  • You have a community• first mindset and enjoy collaborating with othersn  • You are detail• oriented and notice unusual or unexpected behaviorn  • You enjoy solving problems and assessing complex situations to support decisions",
    "courseFees": "The course fees for a SOC Analyst vary based on the provider and location, ranging from approximately INR 10,000 to 2,50,000. In India, standard training typically costs between INR 20,000 and 60,000, while specialized or bootcamp programs can range from INR 50,000 to 3,00,000. Globally, specialized programs may cost around $1,600, while self• paced certifications like the Google Cybersecurity Certificate are available for approximately $49 (INR 3,200) per month.",
    "scholarships": "Kishore Vaigyanik Protsahan Yojana Scholarship: Provided to students in their first year of an engineering undergraduate course with a strong aptitude for scientific research.n• Merit• cum• Means based Scholarship: About 20,000 scholarships awarded by the Ministry of Minority Affairs to cover full course fees for engineering students from minority communities.n• FS• ISAC Future Leaders in Cyber Scholarship: A $10,000 merit• based award for students pursuing cybersecurity careers in financial services, including mentorship and networking opportunities.n• EC• Council CCT Scholarship: A $7 million global initiative providing entry• level technical training and certification resources for aspiring Cyber Security Technicians.n• Paller Cybersecurity Scholarship: A fully funded international program through the SANS Technology Institute for both newcomers and experienced professionals to earn globally recognized credentials online.n• Google Cybersecurity Professional Certificate Scholarship: Offered through CareerCircle and Grow with Google to provide full scholarships for the Google Cybersecurity Professional Certificate.n• WiCyS Security Training Scholarship: A multi• tiered program for WiCyS members that provides advanced SANS training, GIAC certifications, and conference scholarships.n• CyberCorps Scholarship for Service (SFS): Provides full tuition, professional allowances, and stipends ($27,000• $37,000) for cybersecurity students in exchange for post• graduation government service.n• Microsoft Cybersecurity Scholarship Program: Offers financial assistance (up to $500) or certification exam subsidies (up to $375) for community college students.n• KnowBe4 Women in Cybersecurity Scholarship: A $10,000 award for tuition and fees that includes a three• month paid internship.n• (ISC)2 Scholarships: Undergraduate and graduate awards ranging from $1,000 to $5,000 for students studying cybersecurity or information assurance.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, or a related field to build a strong foundation in networking, operating systems, and security basics.n2.  Gain foundational knowledge in networking fundamentals (TCP/IP, DNS, firewalls), operating systems (Windows and Linux), and security principles (CIA triad, encryption).n3.  Obtain entry• level certifications such as CompTIA Security+, CompTIA Network+, or Certified SOC Analyst (CSA) to demonstrate core competency.n4.  Acquire hands• on experience through home labs (using tools like Splunk or Security Onion), CTF challenges, or platforms like TryHackMe and HackTheBox to practice threat detection and log analysis.n5.  Apply for entry• level roles such as IT Helpdesk or Junior SOC Analyst (Tier 1) to gain real• world experience in monitoring alerts and incident triage.n6.  Pursue intermediate certifications like CompTIA CySA+, Certified Ethical Hacker (CEH), or OffSec Defense Analyst (OSDA) to advance to Tier 2 or Tier 3 roles.n7.  Specialize in areas like Digital Forensics, Threat Intelligence, or Malware Analysis by obtaining advanced certifications such as GCIA, GCIH, or CRISC.",
