    "workLocation": "Places of Work: Private Offices, Factories, On• Field, Laboratories, Government Agencies, Nonprofits, Private Companies, and Remote Settings.nnWork Environment: Systems engineers typically work in office environments but frequently visit facilities and job sites, such as manufacturing lines, server storage areas, or construction sites, to inspect processes. They use specialized technology and modeling software regularly. While they generally work full• time during normal business hours, overtime may be required to meet project deadlines. The role often involves working in a matrix managed organization, collaborating with diverse teams including other engineers, researchers, salespeople, and clients. Travel may be necessary to agricultural, industrial, or government settings depending on the specific industry.",
