    "scholarships": "• Google Career Certificate Scholarship: This fully funded program is sponsored by the Tech Incubator at Queens College and offers flexible online training in UX design through Coursera. It is open to anyone with no degree or prior experience required.n  • Diversify Design Scholarship: Designlab offers scholarships worth 50% of UX Academy tuition or $1,000 to aspiring designers from underrepresented groups, including BIPOC, LGBTQ+, and people with disabilities.n  • Project• 100 by Paddicode: This scholarship provides a fully funded UI/UX Certificate program including live online classes, mentorship, and portfolio• building resources for 50 diverse individuals.n  • UX Design Scholarship by DesCan Foundation: A $500 award for third or fourth• year undergraduate design students in Canada who demonstrate passion and proficiency in user experience design.n  • PAVE Scholarship + Experience: These awards provide cash grants and industry mentorship for students in UX Design, retail, and spatial design, with specific opportunities like the ChangeUp and Bish Creative scholarships.n  • AIGA Worldstudio D×D Scholarships: National scholarships for U.S. design students that explicitly include interaction and communication design majors.n  • UX Content Design Training Grants: UX Content Collective offers grants covering 30% to 100% of course prices for university students and marginalized communities globally.n  • UT Dallas Applied Experience Design & Research Scholarship: Financial aid specifically for undergraduate students focused on experience design and research.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Earn a Bachelor's degree in a related field such as Psychology, Human• Computer Interaction (HCI), Computer Science, Statistics, Anthropology, or Social Sciences.n2.  Consider a Master's degree or PhD in HCI, Applied Psychology, Human Factors, or Cognitive Science to gain advanced research skills and a competitive edge.n3.  Supplement formal education with specialized UX research certifications from providers like Google (Coursera), Nielsen Norman Group, or Interaction Design Foundation.n4.  Gain hands• on experience through internships, research assistantships in academic labs, or by volunteering for non• profits and local businesses.n5.  Build a portfolio that demonstrates your proficiency in research methods like user interviews, usability testing, surveys, and data analysis.n6.  Network within the UX community by joining online groups on LinkedIn or Reddit and attending industry meetups and conferences.",
