    "scholarships": "• Bien Motion Design x School of Motion Scholarships: Eight scholarships for underrepresented students to receive education in commercial animation.n  • School of Motion Community Inclusion Scholarship: Provides free places on motion design courses for individuals from underrepresented groups.n  • American Graphic Institute Design Thinking Scholarship: Awarded annually to both part• time and full• time students pursuing careers in design.n  • AIGA Worldstudio DxD Scholarships: Supports minority and economically disadvantaged students in visual communication, including graphic design and illustration.n  • CTN Foundation Scholarships: Includes various awards such as the Torsten Schrank Design Scholarship for character design and the Mary Blair Legacy Scholarship for women designers in animation and illustration.n  • Animation Career Review Scholarship: A merit• based program for students pursuing careers in animation to help with tuition costs.n  • Women in Animation (WIA) Scholarship: Supports female and non• binary students studying animation.n  • ASIFA• Hollywood Animation Educators Forum Scholarships: Provides $2,500 to $5,000 for students in animation• related studies.n  • KIL N.Y.C. Scholarship: A $1,000 award for high school or college students pursuing a career in design.n  • Carlynn's Comic Scholarship: A $1,300 award for students whose lives have been shaped by comics or animation.n  • ESA Foundation Computer and Video Game Arts and Sciences Scholarship: Available for women and underrepresented students in game art and animation.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Earn a bachelor's degree in computer graphics, art, graphic design, animation, or a related field.n2.  Alternatively, complete an associate degree or certificate program in motion graphics or multimedia arts.n3.  Master industry• standard software like Adobe After Effects, Cinema 4D, Photoshop, and Illustrator.n4.  Build a strong portfolio and a short showreel (under two minutes) to showcase animation and storytelling skills.n5.  Gain practical experience through internships, freelance work, or entry• level positions to refine professional skills.n6.  Consider professional certifications such as Adobe Certified Expert (ACE) in After Effects or Cinema 4D Certification.n7.  Stay updated on evolving industry trends, technologies, and creative communities.",
    "loans": "• Vidyalakshmi, www.vidyalakshmi.co.in, is an portal for students seeking education loan.n Thisn portal has been developed under the guidance ofn the Department of Financial Services, (Ministry ofn Finance), Ministry of Education and Indian Banksn Association (IBA).n Some states have student credit cards with lown interest rates, for instance, West Bengal, Odisha,n Bihar, etc.n • All banks give education loans.",
    "careerGrowth": "Junior Motion Designer • Motion Graphics Designer • Senior Motion Designer • Creative Director / Lead",
    "workLocation": "Places of Work: Motion design studios, animation houses, advertising agencies, TV networks, film studios, video game companies, and in• house corporate studios. Work Environment: You will typically work in office settings or creative studios collaborating with production teams. Opportunities for remote work and freelancing from a home office are common in this field.",
    "studyLocation": "This course is offered by the Department of Computer Science and Engineering. This list of institutes is indicative onlynnGOVERNMENT INSTITUTES1.  Savannah College of Art and Design (SCAD), Savannah and Atlanta, Georgian2.  Ringling College of Art and Design, Sarasota, Floridan3.  Rhode Island School of Design (RISD), Providence, Rhode Islandn4.  California Institute of the Arts (CalArts), Valencia, Californian5.  Pratt Institute, Brooklyn, New Yorkn6.  University of Europe for Applied Sciences, Berlin, Germanyn7.  SRH University, Berlin, Germanyn8.  Offenburg University of Applied Sciences, Offenburg, GermanyPRIVATE INSTITUTES1.  School of Visual Arts (SVA), New York City, New Yorkn2.  ArtCenter College of Design, Pasadena, Californian3.  Parsons School of Design, New York City, New Yorkn4.  Otis College of Art and Design, Los Angeles, Californian5.  Rochester Institute of Technology (RIT), Rochester, New Yorkn6.  Full Sail University, Winter Park, Floridan7.  Media Design School (MDS), Auckland, New Zealandn8.  SAE Institute, Berlin, GermanyDISTANCE LEARNING INSTITUTES1.  SCADnow Onlinen2.  School of Motionn3.  Motion Design School",
    "achieverExample": "Arjun Kumar, a prominent Motion Designer from Chennai, has a track record of successfully managing large• scale operations and implementing best practices across his organization."
