    "scholarships": "• AIGA Worldstudio DxD Scholarships: Awarded to students demonstrating a commitment to social change through visual communication, including graphic design.n  • Adobe Design Circle Scholarship: Provides $100,000 for students pursuing design• related fields.n  • Red Egg Marketing Scholarship: A $2,500 award for students interested in careers such as graphic design, web development, and advertising.n  • Print and Graphics Scholarship Foundation: Offers up to $20,000 for students in the graphics industry.n  • Graphic Communications Scholarship Foundation: Supports students pursuing education in the graphic communications media industry.n  • The Doan Foundation For The Arts Scholarship: A $1,500 scholarship for arts and design students.n  • Chris Struthers Memorial Scholarship: Created to uplift and empower the next generation of graphic designers.n  • Al Luna Memorial Design Scholarship: A $1,000 award for BIPOC high school students interested in art or design.n  • Dave Cross Design Arts Scholarship: Available to undergraduate students studying graphic design, media arts, or digital design.n  • Michigan Future of the Arts Scholarship: A $1,000 award for BIPOC students in Michigan pursuing art or design.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 with a focus on basic art and design courses.n2.  Complete a Bachelor's degree in Graphic Design, Fine Arts, or a related field (e.g., Visual Communication, Illustration).n    ORn    Complete an Associate degree in Graphic Design and transfer to a Bachelor's program or pursue entry• level assistant roles.n    ORn    If you already hold a Bachelor's degree in another field, complete a 2 to 3• year technical training program or professional certification in graphic design.n3.  Develop a professional portfolio showcasing creative work and technical proficiency in software like Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign).n4.  Gain experience through internships or junior graphic design roles to progress to mid• level or senior positions such as Art Director or Creative Director.Visit www.scholarships.gov.in for central and state government scholarship schemes. Many institutes also offer merit• based scholarships.nnLOANSnVidyalakshmi (www.vidyalakshmi.co.in) provides a portal to view, apply, and track education loans under government guidance. Several states also offer student credit cards with low interest rates.",
