    "workLocation": "Places of Work: Studios, Ad Agencies, Web/Marketing Firms, Publishers, Retailers, Nonprofit Organizations, Private Offices, Home Offices (Remote). Work Environment: Graphic designers generally work in studios or office environments equipped with computers and software, though many work remotely or as freelancers. The work involves significant time behind a computer, often requires collaboration with clients or design teams, and is subject to frequent time pressure to meet strict deadlines. Opportunities for self• employment and flexible schedules exist.",
    "studyLocation": "This list of institutes is indicative onlynnGOVERNMENT INSTITUTES1.  Indian Institute of Technology, Mumbai, Maharashtran2.  Indian Institute of Technology, Guwahati, Assamn3.  Indian Institute of Technology, Kanpur, Uttar Pradeshn4.  National Institute of Design, Ahmedabad, Gujaratn5.  National Institute of Design, Bengaluru, Karnatakan6.  National Institute of Design, Kurukshetra, Haryanan7.  National Institute of Design, Vijayawada, Andhra PradeshPRIVATE INSTITUTESn(Please check if institute is affiliated and accredited with UGC and AICTE before applying)1.  Shrishti Institute of Art, Design and Technology, Bengaluru, Karnatakan2.  Pearl Academy (Multiple Locations)n3.  World University of Design, Sonipat, Haryanan4.  Symbiosis Institute of Design, Pune, Maharashtran5.  Maeer's MIT Institute of Design, Pune, Maharashtran6.  Indian School of Design and Innovation, Mumbai, Maharashtran7.  Zebra Institute, Kolkata, West Bengaln8.  Dicazo Computer Institute, Jaipur, RajasthanINTERNATIONAL INSTITUTES1.  Rhode Island School of Design (RISD), Providence, USAn2.  Parsons School of Design, New York City, USAn3.  The Pratt Institute, Brooklyn, USAn4.  Maryland Institute College of Art (MICA), Baltimore, USAn5.  California Institute of the Arts (CalArts), Santa Clarita, USAn6.  ArtCenter College of Design, Pasadena, USAn7.  Savannah College of Art and Design (SCAD), USAn8.  University of the Arts London, London, UKONLINE/DISTANCE LEARNING1.  Noble Desktopn2.  Shillington Educationn3.  General Assemblyn4.  New York Institute of Art and Designn5.  Coursera (Google Graphic Design Certificate)n6.  HubSpot Academy",
    "achieverExample": "Rahul Desai, an experienced Graphic Designer from Mumbai, has spent over a decade optimizing processes and leading teams. His recent work focuses on integrating new technologies to improve overall performance."
