    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 with a background in marketing, business, or related fields.n2.  Complete a Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Business Administration (BBA), Communications, or Information Technology.n    ORn    Complete a Master's degree in Digital Marketing, Marketing Management (MBA), or Marketing Analytics for higher• level positions.n3.  Obtain industry certifications such as Google Ads (Search, Display, Video, Shopping, Measurement), Microsoft Advertising, or HubSpot Academy certifications.n4.  Gain practical experience through internships, managing personal blogs, or volunteering for digital marketing roles in societies or non• profits.n5.  Develop technical skills in web analytics (Google Analytics), HTML, CSS, and SEO principles.Visit the National Scholarship Portal (www.scholarships.gov.in) for central and state government schemes. Scholarships like the Indian Oil Educational Scholarship are available for undergraduate students, with a focus on specific demographics.nnLOANSnVidyalakshmi (www.vidyalakshmi.co.in) is the primary portal for education loans under the guidance of the Ministry of Finance and Ministry of Education. Some states also offer student credit cards with low interest rates.nnEntrance exams for higher management studies include CAT, XAT, SNAP, CMAT, and CUET.",
