    "courseFees": "The course fees for a Podcast Producer or Host vary by program and duration:  • AAFT Online Diploma in Podcasting: Rs. 80,000 (with installment options)n  • IAP Career College Podcast Producer Certificate Course: US$ 149.00n  • Noble Desktop Radio and Podcast Production: $1199 + $100 registration feen  • Udemy (Voiceover Masterclass): $84.99n  • European programs: €3700 (5• day) to €6500 (10• day)n  • Captivate Podcast Launch Accelerator: Free",
    "scholarships": "• Podcasting Seriously Awards Fund: Covers submission fees for media/journalism awards and enrollment/registration fees for audio training and education programs for independent BIPOC, Queer, and Trans audio producers.n  • NYC Podcast Awards Scholarships: Provides full fee waivers for award entries to creators who demonstrate financial need.n  • Bob Horner Scholarship: Funds undergraduate scholarships for journalism or communication students, with priority for those pursuing careers in broadcast journalism, video, documentaries, or digital platforms.n  • RTDNA Foundation Scholarships: Open to college students (sophomores, juniors, or seniors) pursuing careers in radio, television, or digital journalism.n  • Della Giustina Scholarship: Available to undergraduate and graduate students pursuing degrees in broadcast or multimedia journalism at any U.S. college or university.n  • pointblank Music School Scholarships: Offers full scholarships for degrees in Music Production & Software Engineering (London) and Music Production & Audio Engineering (Los Angeles).n  • Professional Scholarships by We Are Moving The Needle: Enables creators to attend audio programs globally.n  • College Scholarships by We Are Moving The Needle: Supports creators pursuing degrees in music production, audio engineering, and related fields.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete secondary school. A formal degree is not always required for independent podcasting, but larger news• related entities may require a bachelor's degree in journalism, media production, media arts, or mass communication.n2.  Develop core skills by learning about podcast creation, audio experience, communication, sound design, and project management.n3.  Learn to use industry• standard audio editing software and Digital Audio Workstations (DAW) such as Garageband, Adobe Audition, Audacity, ProTools, Logic Pro X, or Reaper.n4.  Gain hands• on experience by starting an independent podcast, volunteering services for other podcasters, or applying for entry• level roles such as an intern or writer.n5.  Consider specialized training through online platforms like ELVTR, Udemy, Skillshare, LinkedIn Learning, or specific programs like the Podcast Engineering School or IAP Career College.n6.  Build a professional portfolio or reel that showcases technical audio production skills and the ability to generate compelling content.n7.  Network with industry professionals through online groups on Facebook, LinkedIn, or Reddit, and attend industry events to find job opportunities.",
