    "careerGrowth": "Hobbyist Creator • Part• time Creator • Full• time Content Creator • Gaming Influencer • Professional Brand/Business Owner",
    "workLocation": "Places of Work: Private Offices, Home Offices, Gaming Studios, On• field (events). Work Environment: You will typically work from home or in a private office, often at a computer or on a mobile device. Most creators operate independently, though some work within video game companies like Bandai Namco or Nintendo. The role is highly demanding, often requiring a 24/7 commitment with significant time spent on digital platforms like YouTube, Twitch, and TikTok. Travel may be required to attend industry events or meet with brands. Opportunities for remote work and freelancing are common in this field.",
