    "educationPath": "To become a wealth manager, follow these steps:1.  Complete 10+2 in any stream, preferably with a focus on commerce or mathematics.n2.  Earn a bachelor's degree in finance, business administration, economics, accounting, or financial planning.n3.  Obtain entry• level experience in roles such as client service associate, advisor trainee, or junior wealth associate.n4.  Meet licensing and registration requirements, such as FINRA licenses (SIE, Series 7, Series 66/65), depending on your region and role.n5.  Pursue professional certifications like Certified Financial Planner (CFP), Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA), or Chartered Wealth Manager (CWM).n6.  Consider a master's degree (MBA, Master's in Finance, or Master's in Taxation) to advance into senior leadership or work with complex clients.",
