    "studyLocation": "The educational path for a pharmaceutical sales representative typically involves these institutions and programs:nnGOVERNMENT AND ACCREDITED INSTITUTIONS  • University of California San Diego, Skaggs School of Pharmacy and Pharmaceutical Sciences (Drug Commercialization course)n  • Plymouth State University (Undergraduate Certificate in Medical Sales)n  • Accredited colleges and universities offering bachelor's degrees in Biology, Chemistry, Business, Communications, or Health SciencePROFESSIONAL TRAINING AND CERTIFICATION PROVIDERS  • National Association of Pharmaceutical Sales Representatives (CNPR certification)n  • Accreditation Council for Medical Affairs (PRC certification)n  • Medical Sales College (Specialized medical and pharmaceutical sales programs)n  • Manufacturers Representatives Educational Research Foundation (CPMR or CSP certifications)n  • American Pharmaceutical Association (PRC certification)",
