    "traits": "• You like to build or assemble thingsn  • You like to analyse/interpret given informationn  • You like to leadn  • You like to solve problemsn  • You have strong attention to detailn  • You possess a problem• solving mindsetn  • You are a data• driven individualn  • You have a passion for geneticsn  • You work well independently and in teams",
    "courseFees": "The course fees for genomics analysis programs range from free (via YouTube or Coursera trials) to $11,100 for a graduate certificate. Short• term training programs typically cost between INR 2,999 and INR 15,000, while individual online courses and certifications range from approximately $54 to $1,500.",
    "scholarships": "• Post• Baccalaureate Genomics Analyst Fellowship: A two• year program for recent graduates with a $45,500 annual salary and benefits. It offers training in scientific program management, public policy, and science communication at NHGRI or ASHG.n  • NIH Undergraduate Scholarship Program: Provides up to $20,000 per academic year for tuition and living expenses for students from disadvantaged backgrounds committed to biomedical research careers.n  • Genomics• Online Annual University Scholarship: Awarded $1,000 twice a year to students majoring in life sciences who submit an essay on their career goals and favorite scientific discovery.n  • Alliance for Genetic Counseling Fellowship: Offers two• year full scholarships covering tuition, fees, and health insurance, plus a living expense fellowship for students pursuing a Master's degree in Genetic Counseling.n  • Human Genetics Scholar Initiative (HGSI): A professional development program providing membership, travel support, and mentorship for early• career researchers in human genetics and genomics.n  • GeneTex Scholarship Program: A $2,000 scholarship awarded to students in the life sciences.n  • Power Life Sciences Scholarship: A $2,000 award for students pursuing degrees in life science fields.n  • Keystone Symposia Scholarships: Offers $1,200 travel awards for genomics majors to attend professional scientific conferences.n  • FIU Center for Genomic Research Scholarship: Provides a $2,000 award and research experience for advanced undergraduate and master's students.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in the Science stream.n2.  Obtain a Bachelor's degree (BA or BS) in Biology, Genetics, Bioinformatics, Computer Science, or a related biological/computational science field.n3.  Optional: Pursue a Master's degree or Doctorate (PhD) in Genetics, Genomics, or Bioinformatics to advance to research or specialist roles.n4.  Alternatively: Complete a post• baccalaureate certificate program in Genetics, Genomics, or Bioinformatics (typically 1• 2 years).n5.  Develop technical proficiency in programming languages (Python, R, Linux/Bash) and bioinformatics tools (DNA sequencing analysis, RNA• seq).n6.  Gain practical experience through internships, research projects, or fellowships, such as the Post• Baccalaureate Genomics Analyst Fellowship.",
