    "courseFees": "Biotechnology course fees generally range from INR 360 to INR 13 Lakh, depending on the level of study, institution type, and mode of education. For distance learning programs, annual fees typically range between INR 25,000 and INR 35,000. Certificate programs can range from INR 9,000 to INR 18,000, while online degree programs may cost between $15,000 and $40,000 total.",
    "scholarships": "• Gates Cambridge Scholarship: This scholarship supports postgraduate students at the University of Cambridge in fields like biotechnology and biomedical science. It provides full coverage for tuition, living expenses, travel, and research costs for international students.n  • DAAD Scholarships: Offered by the German Academic Exchange Service, these scholarships support international students pursuing master's or PhD programs in biotechnology and related life sciences in Germany.n  • MEXT Scholarship: This Japanese government scholarship covers full tuition, monthly stipends, and travel for international students at the undergraduate, master's, and PhD levels in biotechnology and agricultural biotechnology.n  • Fulbright Foreign Student Scholarship: This program supports international students pursuing master's or PhD degrees in the United States, covering tuition, living expenses, travel, and research costs for fields including bioengineering and genetics.n  • GREAT Scholarship: Funded by the UK government, this scholarship offers partial tuition fee reduction for international students pursuing a master's degree in biotechnology, molecular biology, or bioinformatics at UK universities.n  • Commonwealth Government's Research Training Program (RTP): This program supports students undertaking master's by research or PhD degrees in biotechnology and life sciences in Australia.n  • NSF Graduate Research Fellowship Program: This program supports graduate STEM students in the United States who are pursuing research careers in biotechnology, biomedical science, and genetics.n  • Kishore Vaigyanik Protsahan Yojana Scholarship: Awarded by the Government of India, this scholarship is for engineering students with a strong aptitude for scientific research, covering tuition through an aptitude• based selection.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in the Science stream with Physics, Chemistry, and Biology.n2.  Complete a Bachelor's degree (B.Sc. or B.Tech.) in Biotechnology, Biology, Biochemistry, or Microbiology.n3.  Pursue a Master's degree (M.Sc. or M.Tech.) in Biotechnology or a specialized field like Bioinformatics or Genetics.n4.  For research• intensive roles, complete a Ph.D. in Biotechnology or a related biological science.Scholarships:  • Department of Biotechnology (DBT) Junior Research Fellowship (JRF).n  • CSIR• UGC NET for JRF and Lectureship.n  • Women Scientist Scheme (WOS• A).n  • Biotechnology Ignition Grant (BIG) for entrepreneurs.Entrance Exams:  • GAT• B (Graduate Aptitude Test• Biotechnology).n  • IIT• JAM (Joint Admission test for Masters).n  • CUET• PG for various central universities.n  • GATE (Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering) for M.Tech/Ph.D.n  • JEE Main/Advanced for B.Tech programs in IITs/NITs.Loans:  • Vidyalakshmi portal (www.vidyalakshmi.co.in) for education loans from various banks.n  • State• specific student credit card schemes.",
