    "courseFees": "Course fees for becoming a Gene Therapy Specialist vary by program type: short online courses range from approximately GBP 280 to GBP 1,195, specialized professional certifications cost between USD 1,025 and USD 2,650, and comprehensive university programs like the PG Certificate at NJIT cost around INR 17,50,114 (approx. USD 18,351) per year. Free introductory modules are also available on platforms like Coursera and Educo Life Sciences.",
    "scholarships": "• ISCT EU Scholarship Program: Provides full tuition for European members to enroll in Master or Specialization degrees in Manufacturing of Advanced Therapy Medicinal Products at the University of Granada.n  • UC Davis Cell and Gene Therapy Manufacturing Scholarship: Funded by NIIMBL, this covers the full cost ($6,000) of specialized study program courses and bootcamps, including travel and lodging.n  • GeneTex Scholarship Program: Awards a $2,000 scholarship twice a year to students pursuing STEM undergraduate or graduate degrees, including those in life sciences.n  • NHLI Master's Scholarships: Offered by Imperial College London for the MSc in Genes, Drugs and Stem Cells • Novel Therapies, covering either 50% (£8,150) or 100% (£16,300) of home tuition fees.n  • BSGCT Undergraduate Research Bursary: Provides £250 per week for up to 8 weeks for undergraduates to conduct research in gene and cell therapy laboratories.n  • RARE Scholars Program: Awarded by BioMarin to students living with rare genetic conditions; provides up to $10,000 for four• year programs and $5,000 for two• year or vocational studies.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete 10+2 in the Science stream with a focus on biology and chemistry.n2.  Earn a Bachelor's degree in Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or Molecular Biology.n3.  Gain hands• on experience through laboratory internships, research projects, or wet lab work during undergraduate studies.n4.  Pursue a Master's degree in Cell and Gene Therapy, Human Genetics and Genomics, or a related field for specialized industry roles.n5.  For high• level research, academic faculty positions, or leadership roles, complete a Ph.D. focusing on gene therapy technologies and applications.n6.  For clinical roles working directly with patients, earn a Medical Degree (M.D. or D.O.) followed by a residency and board certification in medical genetics.n7.  Complete postdoctoral research or specialized fellowships to deepen expertise in areas like gene editing or vector development.n8.  Obtain necessary professional certifications or licensure, such as the American Board of Genetic Counseling (ABGC) exam for counselors or board certification for clinical geneticists.",
