    "scholarships": "• National Quantum Scholarships Scheme (NQSS): Master's and PhD scholarships for quantum research or engineering in Singapore, including full tuition and stipends.n  • QuTech Scholarships: Full tuition and living expenses for MSc students at TU Delft specializing in quantum roadmaps.n  • CQA Masters Scholarships: Up to 10 fellowships covering matriculation fees for quantum• related master's programs in Catalonia.n  • RWTH Quantum Technology Scholarship: Full two• year scholarships for the Quantum Technology Master Track at RWTH Aachen University.n  • SandboxAQ Scholarships: Research Excellence ($10,000) and Global Travel ($5,000) awards for PhD students in AI and quantum technology.n  • The Joel Tendler Quantum Responsibility Scholarship: A $5,000 prize for an essay on the ethical implications of quantum computing.n  • CU Boulder Quantum Scholars: Program for undergraduate students at the University of Colorado Boulder.n  • Colorado School of Mines Quantum Engineering Fellowship: Funding for students in the quantum engineering path.n  • ARC Training Centre for Current and Emergent Quantum Technologies Scholarships: PhD stipends of $36,161 plus a $10,000 top• up for research in Australia.n  • Reliance Foundation Postgraduate Scholarships: Up to INR 6 Lakhs for postgraduate students in India in fields including Computer Science and Mathematics & Computing.n  • Kishore Vaigyanik Protsahan Yojana (KVPY) Scholarship: For first• year engineering students with a strong aptitude for scientific research in India.",
    "educationPath": "1.  Complete a Bachelor's degree in a STEM discipline such as Physics, Computer Science, Mathematics, Electrical Engineering, or Quantum Engineering.n2.  Develop essential skills in linear algebra, probability, complex numbers, and programming (specifically Python, C++, and Qiskit).n3.  Consider pursuing a Master's or PhD in Quantum Computing, Quantum Information, Physics, or Computer Engineering for specialized research or hardware roles.n4.  Gain practical experience through research projects, university labs, internships at quantum computing firms, or by participating in quantum hackathons.n5.  Explore specialized certifications or online courses from platforms like IBM (Qiskit), edX, or Coursera to build a portfolio.n6.  For hardware• specific paths, focus on electronics, digital logic, and cryogenic measurement systems. For software paths, focus on quantum algorithms, error correction, and software engineering.",
